\description{
\code{RSConcreteDictionary} is the internal storage adapter shared by
\link{RSDictionary} and \link{RSMutableDictionary}. It lazily owns an external pointer
to a C++ \code{NativeDictionary} and keeps all Rcpp bridge calls out of the public
dictionary classes.
The native table calls each key's \code{hash()} and \code{isEqual()} methods for
lookup; keys must keep their hash and equality state stable while stored.

This class provides storage semantics only. It does not inherit from
\link{RSObject}, copy keys, translate \code{NULL} to \link{RSNull}, or impose mutable versus
immutable behavior. Those responsibilities belong to the public dictionary
wrappers.
}
\section{Methods}{

\itemize{
\item \code{duplicate()} returns an independent shallow copy of the native storage.
\item \code{set(key, value)} inserts or replaces a value.
\item \code{get(key)} returns the value for a key, or \code{NULL} when absent.
\item \code{contains(key)} reports whether a key is present.
\item \code{remove(key)} removes a key and reports whether it existed.
\item \code{clear()} removes every entry.
\item \code{keys()} and \code{values()} return the stored objects as lists.
\item \code{entries()} returns corresponding key-value pairs as two-element lists.
\item \code{count()} returns the number of entries.
\item \code{contentHash()} returns an order-independent aggregate hash of the keys.
\item \code{prepareForSerialization()} captures a temporary R snapshot used only to
rebuild the native table after deserialization.
}
}

